      },
      "message": "fix(app): a probe searches a short way past the face and feeds below the safe plane\n\nFound on a real Tormach 770MX (#521's hands-on test): a new Probe op\nsearched 5 mm past the expected face (G38.2 Z-0.1969), deep enough to\nbottom a stylus when the face is missing, and rapided straight down to\nthe approach point over the part.\n\n- A new Probe op's probe distance is max(2 x tolerance, 1 mm) (1 mm for\n  the seeded tolerance); existing documents keep their stated value.\n- A probe distance past 2 mm draws a named, non-blocking\n  Warning::ProbeSearch (the post is not held).\n- The probe cycle opens with a positioning rapid that ends at the safe\n  plane, then FEEDS down to the approach point: no probe rapid runs\n  below the safe plane. Fanuc probe goldens gain that line.\n- The probe page's hint says the distance is a search limit, not a\n  destination.\n\nPinned by probe_search (3 tests; below_the_safe_plane_a_probe_only_feeds\nfails on the old cycle).\n\nFixes #570\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
